  "costUsd": null,
  "content": "Putting is the clearest team-wide leak right now. Every player with recorded rounds is losing strokes on the green, and by a wider margin than any other skill area.\n\n**Strokes gained putting** (same window per player, 14–23 rounds each, May–Sept 2026):\n- Owen Carter: -2.16\n- Ethan Park: -2.72\n- Cole Bennett: -2.93\n- Mason Rivers: -3.00\n- Dylan Brooks: -3.00\n- Tyler Hayes: -3.34\n- Jackson Hale: -3.91\n\nFor comparison, strokes gained approach over the same stretch ranges from -0.83 (Cole Bennett) to -3.83 (Owen Carter) — a wider spread, but the team average loss there (~-2.3) is smaller than putting's (~-3.0). Off the tee, five of seven players are net positive, and around-the-green is split roughly even — neither is the drag that putting is.\n\nCoverage note: 7 of your 8 active players have recorded rounds in this window; Audit Testplayer has none.\n\nThis lines up with what's already flagged individually — you've got active focus areas on lag putting / 3-putt chains for Cole Bennett, Jackson Hale, and Dylan Brooks, plus short-putt make-rate work for Cole (3-5ft) and Owen (5-10ft). A team putting session this week — green reading and distance control on 15-30ft lags to cut the 3-putt chain, plus makeable-range reps (3-10ft) — would hit the biggest collective number and reinforce what's already being tracked for three of your players.",
